# Source trees for compiled tools — owned by their Cargo/etc projects, not
# copied into $HOME. Templates and run_onchange hooks read these via `include`,
# which works regardless of this ignore.
src

# Repo's own documentation and tooling. These are read from $DOTFILES by the
# scripts that need them (dot-doctor resolves $DOTFILES/checks,
# dot-install-zsh-plugins resolves $DOTFILES/plugins.lock — verified, nothing
# reads them from $HOME), so copying them into the home directory served no
# purpose. Worse, it made `chezmoi status` list a dozen repo files as drifted
# targets, burying the drift that actually matters.
# These source-root names do not collide with nested managed config paths.
.github
AGENTS.md
CLAUDE.md
LICENSE
PERF.md
README.md
checks
docs
plugins.bin
plugins.lock
renovate.json
scripts
